This product includes original skill guidance, deterministic transcript
parsing / structure annotation / template distillation scripts, and
evaluation artifacts released under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Methodology note: the four-part structure vocabulary (hook / build /
twist / cta) reflects common Chinese short-video practice; the practice of
converting duration ratios into second-level beat points is inspired by
published screenwriting beat-sheet methods. These names and methods are
referenced for description only; no third-party material is redistributed.

All evaluation fixtures (transcripts, annotations, template seeds) are
synthetic and written by hand for this repository. No real video script,
transcript, or creator content is included, and nothing here scores or
rates content quality.

Real-input evaluation (v0.3.0): the parsing layer was also run on a Whisper
transcription of the first 90 seconds of "Zh-规则怪谈.ogg" from Wikimedia
Commons (CC BY-SA 4.0; https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zh-%E8%A7%84%E5%88%99%E6%80%AA%E8%B0%88.ogg).
Neither the audio nor its transcript is redistributed here; only aggregate
statistics (cue counts, block counts, block durations) are stored in
evals/runs_v2/real_whisper_stats.json.

Thresholds and metrics cite public sources (Netflix Timed Text Style Guides,
W3C WebVTT, TikTok creative best practices, Pevzner & Hearst 2002 WindowDiff,
Cohen's kappa with Landis & Koch 1977 bands); see references/benchmarks.md.
These are referenced for description only; no third-party text is
redistributed.
